{
  "_meta": {
    "title": "Mahan Kosh shorthand legend (ਸੰਕੇਤ)",
    "parse_version": "1.1.0",
    "parse_version_note": "Bump on ANY change to parse behavior — parser code (parse_shorthand.py) or legend data in this file. Stamped into every parsed sense; /health counts rows whose stamp differs (expected 0). After bumping: python3 pipeline/mahan-kosh/parse_shorthand.py --run && npm run ingest:mahankosh (~1 min).",
    "purpose": "Machine-readable key to the abbreviations, markers, and orthographic conventions used inside Mahan Kosh entries, so the pipeline can parse definition_text deterministically (etymology language, POS, citations, cross-references) instead of by ad-hoc substring matching.",
    "sources": {
      "front_matter": {
        "work": "Kahn Singh Nabha, ਗੁਰੁਸ਼ਬਦ ਰਤਨਾਕਰ ਮਹਾਨ ਕੋਸ਼ (Gurushabad Ratnakar Mahan Kosh), 1930",
        "sections": [
          "ਮਹਾਨਕੋਸ਼ ਦੇ ਪਤਿਆਂ ਦੇ ਸੰਖੇਪ ਸੰਕੇਤ (abbreviations of the sources/headings)",
          "ਅੱਖਰਾਂ ਦੇ ਸੰਕੇਤ (signs on letters — Kahn Singh's diacritic system for foreign phonemes)"
        ],
        "witness": "Bhasha Vibhag Punjab reprint scan on Punjabi Wikisource, file 'ਮਹਾਨ ਕੋਸ਼ ਭਾਗ 1.pdf', PDF pages 19-21 (front-matter pages ੲ, ਅ, ...)",
        "witness_urls": [
          "https://pa.wikisource.org/wiki/ਪੰਨਾ:ਮਹਾਨ_ਕੋਸ਼_ਭਾਗ_1.pdf/19",
          "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ਮਹਾਨ_ਕੋਸ਼_ਭਾਗ_1.pdf"
        ],
        "verified": "2026-08-03: transcribed directly from the scan page images (pages 20-21 have no Wikisource transcription yet; page 19's transcription is unproofread and was corrected against the image)"
      },
      "corpus": {
        "file": "pipeline/mahan-kosh/output/entries.jsonl",
        "scope": "12,772 found entries / 23,092 senses scraped from the searchgurbani.com Mahan Kosh API",
        "analyzed": "2026-08-03 via pipeline/mahan-kosh/analyze_shorthand.py"
      }
    },
    "source_values": {
      "front_matter": "listed in the book's own printed abbreviation key (citation above)",
      "corpus": "not in the printed key; inferred from consistent usage in the scraped corpus (best-judgment, flagged per the provenance principle)"
    },
    "notes": [
      "The scraper's original 7-marker map (pipeline/mahan-kosh/scrape.py extract_cross_refs) includes ਪੰ. (Punjabi), ਉ. (Urdu) and ਦੇਸ਼. (regional) — NONE of these appear in the printed key. The ਉ. marker was already found to be 32/34 false positives (see pipeline/etymology/parse.ts REQUIRES_CORROBORATION); this legend supersedes those three markers.",
      "Short markers (ਸ. ਹੀ. ਪਾ. ਯੂ. ...) are only reliable positionally: at the head of a sense, immediately after a sense number, or immediately before a script run / citation. Bare substring matching over-counts them badly (e.g. ਹੀ. matches inside ਸਹੀ.).",
      "L. doubles as the Latin-language marker and as the prefix of Linnaean binomial species names (e.g. 'L. Vatica Robusta') in flora/fauna entries.",
      "UNICODE NORMALIZATION: the scraped corpus writes nukta letters decomposed (base + U+0A3C), and the precomposed Gurmukhi nukta letters U+0A59–U+0A5E are composition-excluded in NFC. Any parser matching this legend against corpus text MUST normalize both sides (NFD, or an explicit precomposed↔decomposed map) or markers like ਫ਼ਾ./ਖ਼ਾ. silently fail to match."
    ]
  },

